# PHP Insecure Deserialization - Privilege Escalation via Client-Side Serialized Session Cookie

---

# Executive Summary

A privilege escalation vulnerability was identified in the application's session management mechanism. The application stored user authorization data inside a client-side PHP serialized object without any integrity protection (such as an HMAC or digital signature).

By modifying the serialized object's `admin` attribute from `false` to `true`, it was possible to obtain administrator privileges and access restricted functionality, including the ability to delete arbitrary user accounts.

