# Affected Endpoints

```http
GET /my-account
```

```http
GET /admin
```

```http
GET /admin/delete?username=carlos
```

---

# Description

The application stores authenticated user information inside a **serialized PHP object** contained in the `session` cookie.

The cookie includes an authorization property named `admin`.

Because the application deserializes the object received from the client **without validating its integrity**, an attacker can modify the authorization flag and gain administrator privileges.

---

# Root Cause

The server stores authorization data on the client side instead of maintaining it server side.

Furthermore, the serialized object is:

- Not digitally signed
- Not protected with an HMAC
- Not encrypted

As a result, any authenticated user can modify the serialized object before sending it back to the server.

