# Conclusion

The application trusted a client-controlled serialized PHP object to determine user privileges. Because the session cookie lacked integrity protection, modifying a single boolean value (`admin`) from `false` to `true` resulted in full administrative access.

This vulnerability demonstrates a classic case of **Insecure Deserialization** combined with **Broken Access Control**, where sensitive authorization decisions are delegated to data fully controlled by the client.
